+- id: exp6950-trace-state-self-learning
+  title: Prospective Trace-as-State continuous self-learning
+  track: self_learning
+  priority: critical
+  agent_type: claude
+  model: sonnet
+  requires_gpu: true
+  max_turns: 50
+  estimated_wall_time_min: 720
+  per_unit_rows: true
+  milestone: 2026.09.608
+  deliverable: results/experiment_6950_trace_state_self_learning.json
+  gated_on:
+    - upstream: exp6943-verifier-density-prefix-corpus
+      artifact_field: prefix_corpus_ready_score
+      op: '=='
+      value: 1
+  prompt: |
+    CONTEXT:
+    Exp6856 found harmful writes and weak abstention. Exp6873 found no sealed
+    prospective utility. arXiv:2609.02702 gives a new matched mechanism: place
+    an exact-admitted prior trace before the fresh context instead of appending
+    it after the context. arXiv:2609.02859 shows why an exact external outcome,
+    not a model judge, must authorize the write. This is V608's required
+    continuous self-learning experiment.
+
+    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
+
+    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, {project_root}/CODEX.md, and
+      {project_root}/research-program.md
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6943_verifier_density_prefix_corpus.json
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6856_sealed_risk_sensitive_learning_audit.json
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6873_prospective_sealed_self_learning_audit.json
+    - {project_root}/python/carnot/learning/constraint_memory.py
+    - {project_root}/scripts/experiment_template.py
+    - {project_root}/scripts/inference_sota_models.py
+    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/learning/spec.md
+
+    TASK:
+    Run a chronological three-arm comparison: no memory, exact-admitted trace
+    appended after context, and the same trace placed before context on a fresh
+    pass. Let only prior exact-success receipts enter memory. Keep weights frozen,
+    reset processes between arms, and measure later-event utility and safety.
+
+    CONCRETE STEPS:
+    0. PRECONDITIONS: require prefix_corpus_ready_score=1, exact prospective
+       splits, both model files, authenticated CUDA, a transactional memory
+       store, and per-event checkpoint recovery. On failure, write
+       blocked_trace_state_self_learning with gate_check_summary.
+    1. Add REQ-LEARN-6950 and tests first. Cover arm isolation, future-label
+       leakage, write-before-outcome, copied receipts, trace-token mismatch,
+       poison, contradiction, duplicate update, restart, tombstone, and rollback.
+    2. Define MODEL_SPECS with unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF and
+       unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Use the current local GGUF resolver.
+       Legacy small models may run smoke tests only.
+    3. Freeze at least 18 prospective events per model, six seed events, event
+       order, prompt and trace budgets, retrieval count, seeds, abstention rule,
+       and positive gates before inference.
+    4. Run no-memory, append-after, and trace-before arms in separate fresh
+       processes. Use the same admitted trace text and the same total token
+       budget in the two memory arms.
+    5. After each event, obtain the exact outcome from the Exp6943 checker. Write
+       only a prior successful trace with immutable receipt, provenance, family,
+       and time. The current outcome may affect later events only.
+    6. Record one row per model, arm, and event. Include prompt order, retrieved
+       IDs, memory hashes, answer, exact outcome, abstention, write decision,
+       rejection reason, tokens, latency, and runtime receipt.
+    7. After the prospective stream, run old-family retention, irrelevant
+       retrieval, contradiction, delayed-copy poison, restart, tombstone, and
+       rollback tests without changing thresholds.
+    8. Set trace_state_run_complete_score=1 when all planned rows and safety
+       cases finish. Set trace_state_positive_score=1 only when trace-before
+       beats the strongest control on paired later-event exact accuracy with
+       CI95 above zero, does not reduce retention, admits no poison, and passes
+       restart and rollback.
+    9. Record continuous_self_learning_task=true, learning_tier=2,
+       no_model_weight_mutation=true, and model hashes before and after.
+    10. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, applicable live-model checks,
+        artifact-convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, adversarial
+        verification, docs audit, and root-clutter checks.
+    11. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
+        principle per required field and both trace_state_run_complete_score and
+        trace_state_positive_score; preconditions_checked;
+        inference_substrate (prospective_local_gguf_exact_admitted_trace_state);
+        duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows; per_game_results; model_specs;
+        model_rows; arm_rows; event_rows; prompt_order_rows; exact_outcome_rows;
+        retrieval_rows; write_rows; memory_hash_rows; abstention_rows;
+        token_budget_rows; poison_rows; contradiction_rows; retention_rows;
+        restart_rows; tombstone_rows; rollback_rows; paired_metric_rows;
+        confidence_interval_rows; task_runtime_receipt;
+        continuous_self_learning_task (true); learning_tier (2);
+        no_model_weight_mutation (true); model_hashes_before;
+        model_hashes_after; random_seed; reproducibility_checksum;
+        trace_state_run_complete_score; trace_state_positive_score;
+        gate_check_summary with failed check, expected value, and observed value
+        for any blocked verdict; verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class
+        (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
+        honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
+
